DevOps Interview Command Series — Jira & Confluence (Day 5) 📘

Jira and Confluence are core tools for DevOps collaboration.
From Agile planning, incident tracking, change management, to documentation & runbooks — DevOps teams rely on them daily.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Jira & Confluence commands / operations you must know:

# Jira (via REST API / practical usage)
curl -u user:api_token \
 -X GET https://jira_url/rest/api/2/project

curl -u user:api_token \
 -X GET https://jira_url/rest/api/2/issue/ISSUE-KEY

curl -u user:api_token \
 -X POST https://jira_url/rest/api/2/issue \
 -H "Content-Type: application/json"

# Common Jira JQL
project = DEVOPS AND status = "In Progress"
assignee = currentUser()
status CHANGED DURING (-1d, now())
priority = High ORDER BY created DESC

# Confluence (REST API)
curl -u user:api_token \
 -X GET https://confluence_url/rest/api/content

curl -u user:api_token \
 -X POST https://confluence_url/rest/api/content


🎯 Interview Focus
• Agile workflow understanding (Scrum / Kanban)
• Incident, bug & change tracking
• Writing RCA & postmortems
• Maintaining runbooks & SOPs
• Integration with CI/CD pipelines
